   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Be_Seeing_You",
   "resumo_en": "Be Seeing You was the fifth album by Dr. Feelgood, released in October 1977. After the departure of Wilko Johnson, this was Dr. Feelgood's first album with guitarist Gypie Mayo.\nThe album reached number 55 in the UK Albums Chart in October 1977, and remained in that chart for only three weeks. It spawned their second single to enter the corresponding UK Singles Chart - \"She's A Wind Up\".\nThe album's title was a catchphrase, used by the band, taken from the cult TV series, The Prisoner, which was enjoying a revival at the time.  This theme continued on the album sleeve with the line \"produced by Number 2 for Number 6\", and included photos of the band in piped blazers and scarves, similar to those used in the series, and some \"penny farthing\" badges, although the album's front cover was photographed in the band's local pub, the Admiral Jellicoe.",
